1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,280
Hello everyone, and welcome to Two Cups English.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,720
I'm Mia, and Ben is here with me.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,580
This podcast is for people who are learning English.

4
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:11,080
We speak slowly.

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:12,980
We use simple words.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,419
And we repeat the important words many times.

7
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,630
Today, our topic is kindness.

8
00:00:20,330 --> 00:00:22,300
Not kindness to other people.

9
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:23,620
Kindness to yourself.

10
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,740
Ben, did you make a mistake this week?

11
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:28,820
Hi Mia.

12
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:29,390
Hi everyone.

13
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:31,200
Yes, I did.

14
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:35,140
On Tuesday, I forgot a meeting.

15
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,960
Completely.

16
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,020
My colleague called me, and I was at home, making soup.

17
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:47,210
And for the rest of the day, a voice in my head said, "You are so lazy.

18
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:51,400
You always do this." What about you, Mia?

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:52,510
Any mistakes?

20
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:54,720
One, Ben.

21
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:58,620
Yesterday, I sent an email to the wrong person.

22
00:00:58,760 --> 00:00:59,480
A small mistake.

23
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:00,900
Nobody was angry.

24
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:02,980
It was fixed in five minutes.

25
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:08,360
But for the rest of the day, my voice said, "You are so stupid.

26
00:01:08,860 --> 00:01:12,240
You are not good at your job." All day.

27
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:14,360
For a five-minute mistake.

28
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:17,680
All day, for five minutes, Mia.

29
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:19,940
That is a bad trade.

30
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:21,940
And that voice.

31
00:01:22,890 --> 00:01:26,440
"You are so stupid." I know that voice.

32
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:28,039
Where does it come from?

33
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,800
I think the voice is old, Ben.

34
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,900
It started at school, maybe.

35
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,100
A teacher.

36
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,060
A parent.

37
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,120
A test.

38
00:01:36,860 --> 00:01:40,670
Somebody said, "You can do better," and the voice learned it.

39
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:44,950
And now it says it every day, even when nobody else does.

40
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:49,540
It is the least kind person I know, and it lives in my head.

41
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:58,120
"The least kind person I know, and it lives in my head." Mia, that is our topic today.

42
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,220
So here is our plan.

43
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:04,580
In part one, we talk about our own voices.

44
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:06,160
What they say, and when.

45
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:12,260
In part two, we ask why kindness to yourself works better than the hard voice.

46
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:14,880
And I have a true story for that.

47
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,860
In part three, we share simple ways to talk to yourself like a friend.

48
00:02:20,870 --> 00:02:22,560
Does that sound good?

49
00:02:22,570 --> 00:02:24,240
That sounds good, Ben.

50
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:28,049
And to everyone listening, please do not worry if you miss something.

51
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,140
You will hear it again.

52
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:34,549
You can listen while you walk, while you cook, or while you have a hard day.

53
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:38,560
And if today is a hard day, this episode is for you.

54
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,160
Okay, Ben.

55
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,060
Part one.

56
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:44,880
Your voice says "lazy." Tell me more about it.

57
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,940
My voice does not say "stupid," Mia.

58
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:59,540
It says "lazy." "You should have done more today." "Other people work harder." "You are wasting your life." And the strange thing is this.

59
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:13,060
If my friend worked all day, made a soup, and called his mother, I would say, "That is a good day." But the voice says to me, "You did nothing." Same day.

60
00:03:13,700 --> 00:03:14,460
Different judge.

61
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,280
"Same day.

62
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:19,960
Different judge." Ben, that is exactly it.

63
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,720
Can I tell you about the moment I noticed this?

64
00:03:23,440 --> 00:03:25,350
It was last year, with my friend Anna.

65
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,280
Anna, from the café?

66
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:28,569
I remember her.

67
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,040
She is the one who always laughs first.

68
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:33,500
What happened, Mia?

69
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,860
She failed her driving test, Ben.

70
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,400
She called me, crying.

71
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:40,980
And I said, "Anna, one test is one test.

72
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:43,320
You drove well for months.

73
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,360
You will pass next time.

74
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:48,800
Be kind to yourself tonight." I meant every word.

75
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,219
That is a good friend, Mia.

76
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:51,990
A real friend.

77
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,530
And after the call?

78
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:57,280
After the call, I sat there, Ben.

79
00:03:57,810 --> 00:04:05,310
And I thought, "I failed my driving test twice, and I called myself a failure for a year." Same words.

80
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:06,400
Same test.

81
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,060
Kind to Anna.

82
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,560
Cruel to me.

83
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:12,560
And I did not even see it until that call.

84
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,780
Kind to Anna, cruel to you.

85
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,480
Mia, I think everyone does this.

86
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,060
We have two languages.

87
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:22,800
One for friends, one for ourselves.

88
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:25,420
We forgive a friend's mistake in one minute.

89
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:27,720
We punish our own mistake for a year.

90
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,620
One minute is enough for a friend's mistake.

91
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,160
Why not for ours?

92
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,180
And what did you do after the driving tests?

93
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,360
Did you try again?

94
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,060
No, Ben.

95
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:39,620
That is the sad part.

96
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,480
I avoided driving for a year.

97
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:44,840
Not because I was kind to myself.

98
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:48,020
Because I was cruel, and cruel made me afraid.

99
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:52,610
If somebody shouts at you every time you fail, you stop trying.

100
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:56,180
Even if the somebody is you.

101
00:04:56,190 --> 00:04:59,120
"Even if the somebody is you." Yes, Mia.

102
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,020
I have a story like that too.

103
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,640
Two years ago, I lost a job.

104
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:06,980
And for three weeks, the voice did not stop.

105
00:05:07,070 --> 00:05:07,690
"You failed.

106
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,240
You are not good enough.

107
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:12,670
You will never find another one." Every morning.

108
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:13,760
Every night.

109
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:16,070
Three weeks, Ben.

110
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:20,320
That is a long time to live with that voice every morning.

111
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:22,140
And what did you do in those three weeks?

112
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,760
Nothing, Mia.

113
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,700
I did not apply for any jobs.

114
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:27,380
Not one.

115
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:29,760
Because the voice said there was no point.

116
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:32,200
And then a friend came to visit.

117
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:33,390
And he said one sentence.

118
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,840
"Ben, you lost a job.

119
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,700
You did not lose yourself."

120
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:39,940
"You lost a job.

121
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:44,620
You did not lose yourself." Ben, that is what a friend does.

122
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,740
A friend separates the thing from the person.

123
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:50,200
What happened after that sentence?

124
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:52,100
I cried, Mia.

125
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,660
And the next day, I applied for two jobs.

126
00:05:55,780 --> 00:06:01,389
One sentence, from a kind voice, did in one day what three weeks of the hard voice could not do.

127
00:06:02,580 --> 00:06:05,240
And that is when I started to think about this.

128
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,940
Maybe the hard voice does not work.

129
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,840
Maybe it never worked.

130
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,160
Maybe it never worked.

131
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:18,190
Ben, I want to talk about your friend Tom for a moment, because you told me about him, and he taught me something.

132
00:06:19,580 --> 00:06:20,380
Tom!

133
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,160
Yes.

134
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,960
Tom forgets things, Mia.

135
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,790
Keys, dates, names.

136
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:27,100
And when he forgets, he laughs.

137
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:31,200
He says, "Classic Tom." And then he fixes it.

138
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:32,540
No speech.

139
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:33,700
No punishment.

140
00:06:34,229 --> 00:06:36,290
"Classic Tom," and on with the day.

141
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:40,480
"Classic Tom." I love that, Ben.

142
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,440
It is kind and honest at the same time.

143
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:53,380
It does not say, "I never make mistakes." It says, "I made one, and I am still me." And is Tom lazy about his mistakes?

144
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:54,980
The opposite, Mia.

145
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:57,360
He fixes them faster than I fix mine.

146
00:06:58,060 --> 00:07:01,260
Because he does not spend an hour in the punishment room first.

147
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,610
He goes straight to the fixing.

148
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:06,480
Being kind to himself saves him an hour every time.

149
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:08,040
And the evening, too.

150
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:10,420
The punishment room does not close at five.

151
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,320
It stays open all night.

152
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:15,560
And one hour in that room is enough to ruin a day.

153
00:07:15,589 --> 00:07:20,800
"The punishment room stays open all night." Ben, that is true.

154
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,240
Okay, so that was part one.

155
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:24,200
Our voices.

156
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:31,060
"Stupid" and "lazy," Anna's driving test, a lost job, and Classic Tom.

157
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:33,000
Now, part two.

158
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:36,780
Why does kindness work better than the hard voice?

159
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,520
Ben, you said there is real research.

160
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:40,640
There is, Mia.

161
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:42,199
Okay, part two.

162
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,000
This is a true story.

163
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,900
There is a scientist named Kristin Neff.

164
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:49,300
She works at the University of Texas.

165
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:54,320
In 2003, she started to study something she called self-compassion.

166
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,790
Compassion is kindness for someone who is suffering.

167
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,680
Self-compassion is that same kindness, for yourself.

168
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:05,519
Kindness for yourself, as a science, Ben?

169
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:08,020
I did not know you could measure that.

170
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,200
What did she ask people?

171
00:08:09,670 --> 00:08:10,820
A simple question, Mia.

172
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:15,430
When you fail, do you talk to yourself like a friend, or like an enemy?

173
00:08:16,210 --> 00:08:19,240
And she measured it, in thousands of people.

174
00:08:19,270 --> 00:08:21,660
And what she found surprised a lot of people.

175
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:23,180
What did she find?

176
00:08:23,980 --> 00:08:26,540
I think many people believe the hard voice helps.

177
00:08:27,230 --> 00:08:32,460
"If I am kind to myself, I will become lazy." That is the fear, isn't it?

178
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:33,580
That is the fear, Mia.

179
00:08:34,300 --> 00:08:35,810
But the research found the opposite.

180
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:40,060
People who were kind to themselves after a mistake were less afraid.

181
00:08:40,590 --> 00:08:41,810
They had less anxiety.

182
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,680
And here is the important part.

183
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:49,300
In a later study, in 2012, researchers gave people a hard test.

184
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,200
A hard test, Ben.

185
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:53,780
I already feel nervous for those people.

186
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:55,020
And then?

187
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,200
What happened after they failed?

188
00:08:57,780 --> 00:09:01,120
Some people were told to be kind to themselves after they failed, Mia.

189
00:09:01,850 --> 00:09:04,200
And those people studied more for the next test.

190
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,240
Not less.

191
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:06,240
More.

192
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:09,280
Kindness did not make them lazy.

193
00:09:09,340 --> 00:09:11,320
Kindness made them try again.

194
00:09:11,330 --> 00:09:16,949
"Kindness made them try again." Ben, that is the opposite of what the voice says.

195
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:25,480
The voice says, "If I am hard on you, you will improve." But the hard voice makes me afraid, and afraid people hide.

196
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:26,660
They avoid the test.

197
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,330
Like me, with driving.

198
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:30,780
Like you, with driving, Mia.

199
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:32,830
And like me, with the jobs.

200
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,360
So the question is, how do we change the voice?

201
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:39,650
Because it is old, and it has its own key.

202
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:42,240
Let me tell you what I do.

203
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:46,260
When the voice starts, I say the sentence again, but I put a friend's name in it.

204
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,680
A friend's name, Ben?

205
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,480
How does that work?

206
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:50,500
Any friend?

207
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:53,660
The voice says, "You are lazy," Mia.

208
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:58,250
I say, "Tom is lazy." And immediately, I feel it.

209
00:09:59,060 --> 00:09:59,880
That is not true.

210
00:10:00,360 --> 00:10:02,020
Tom worked all day.

211
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:02,980
Tom made soup.

212
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:04,240
That is enough.

213
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:06,040
Tom is not lazy.

214
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:09,960
And if it is not true for Tom, it is not true for me.

215
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:11,380
Same day.

216
00:10:11,930 --> 00:10:13,360
The name changes the judge.

217
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:17,080
"The name changes the judge." I like that, Ben.

218
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:20,320
I do something similar, but with the friend's face.

219
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:23,840
When the voice comes, I imagine Anna sitting next to me.

220
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:29,140
And I ask, "What would I say to Anna right now?" And the answer comes fast.

221
00:10:29,930 --> 00:10:30,470
"It's okay.

222
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,620
You fixed it.

223
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,540
Have some tea."

224
00:10:34,310 --> 00:10:38,680
"Have some tea." Mia, that is the most Two Cups answer.

225
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,390
And do you say it?

226
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:40,340
Out loud?

227
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,860
Out loud, Ben, if nobody is there.

228
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,710
It feels strange the first time.

229
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:47,980
Like talking to a child.

230
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,860
But maybe that is the point.

231
00:10:50,410 --> 00:10:52,220
The part of me that is hurt is small.

232
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:54,800
And small things need kind words.

233
00:10:55,580 --> 00:11:02,500
"Small things need kind words." Mia, let me talk about the word "mistake," because the voice uses it wrong.

234
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:05,140
A mistake is a thing that happened.

235
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,220
An email to the wrong person.

236
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,560
A wrong turn.

237
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,020
A burned soup.

238
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:13,340
The voice takes the mistake and makes it a person.

239
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:17,900
"You are a mistake." One email becomes a whole life.

240
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,640
But a mistake is not a person, Ben.

241
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:24,060
It is one thing, on one day.

242
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,200
Yesterday, Mia made one mistake.

243
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,220
Mia is not a mistake.

244
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:31,140
Those are two very different sentences.

245
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:32,900
And the voice only knows one of them.

246
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:37,680
"A mistake is a thing, not a person." Mia, write that down.

247
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,840
And there is a second word the voice uses wrong.

248
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:47,700
"Always." "You always do this." "You never learn." Always and never.

249
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:50,040
Those are the voice's favorite words.

250
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:52,580
But I do not live in "always," Ben.

251
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,680
I live in today.

252
00:11:54,740 --> 00:11:56,160
Today I made one mistake.

253
00:11:56,780 --> 00:12:00,200
Today I also finished two reports and helped a new colleague.

254
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:01,880
Today is a mix.

255
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:03,560
Every day is a mix.

256
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:09,320
When I say "today" instead of "always," the mistake becomes one thing in a full day.

257
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:10,900
Not the whole story.

258
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:16,660
"Today, not always." That is a small word change with a big effect, Mia.

259
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:18,440
And one more word.

260
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:22,110
"Enough." The hard voice never says a number.

261
00:12:22,890 --> 00:12:24,409
"Not enough" has no number.

262
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,560
How much English is enough?

263
00:12:27,189 --> 00:12:28,340
How much work is enough?

264
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:29,930
It never says.

265
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:31,620
So we can never reach it.

266
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,420
So what do you do, Ben?

267
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:37,390
When the voice says "not enough" and gives you no number?

268
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:39,100
Today, for example.

269
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:45,020
Today I studied ten minutes, and the voice said, "Not enough." Do you argue with it?

270
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:49,540
I ask it, "How much is enough, then?" And it has no answer, Mia.

271
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:50,860
It never had one.

272
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:54,240
Then I decide the number myself, like a friend would.

273
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:56,760
"You studied twenty minutes today.

274
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:59,550
That is enough for a Tuesday." Twenty minutes.

275
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,110
A Tuesday.

276
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:01,770
Real things.

277
00:13:02,610 --> 00:13:04,380
"The voice lives in fog.

278
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:08,650
Kindness lives in numbers." Ben, I love that.

279
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:11,060
Okay, so that was part two.

280
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,240
Why kindness works.

281
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:14,840
We talked about Kristin Neff and the test.

282
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:17,720
We said kindness made people try again.

283
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:20,500
And we said a mistake is a thing, not a person.

284
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,260
Now, part three.

285
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:25,100
Simple ways to talk to yourself like a friend.

286
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,840
Ben, you go first.

287
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:28,620
Okay, part three.

288
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:31,760
My first idea is for three in the afternoon, Mia.

289
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:34,060
Because that is when my voice is loudest.

290
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:35,500
I look at my list.

291
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:36,830
Half is done.

292
00:13:37,419 --> 00:13:39,080
And the voice says, "Half?

293
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:40,290
Only half?

294
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:44,720
Other people finish everything." So now I look at the done half.

295
00:13:45,320 --> 00:13:46,120
Not the other half.

296
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:51,280
And I say, "That is enough for one morning." Today, half is enough.

297
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:58,700
"Same list, different counting." Ben, my three o'clock voice is about my body.

298
00:13:58,710 --> 00:14:00,140
"You are tired again.

299
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:00,780
You are weak.

300
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:05,020
You should have more energy." As if being tired is a mistake.

301
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:07,100
And what do you say to it now, Mia?

302
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,240
Today, for example.

303
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,150
You look tired today.

304
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,420
What I would say to Anna, Ben.

305
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:14,800
"You are tired because you worked.

306
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:16,420
Sit down for ten minutes.

307
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,040
Ten minutes is enough.

308
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:24,520
Drink some water." And the strange thing is, when I am kind to my tired body, it gets less tired.

309
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:27,200
When I shout at it, it gets more tired.

310
00:14:27,860 --> 00:14:29,580
The body listens to the voice, too.

311
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:35,190
"The body listens to the voice, too." Mia, my second idea is for the evening.

312
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:39,870
At night, in bed, the voice reads everything I did wrong today.

313
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:40,350
Slowly.

314
00:14:40,910 --> 00:14:41,600
With details.

315
00:14:42,519 --> 00:14:43,880
I used to listen to the whole list.

316
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,880
Now I have a small rule.

317
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:48,780
When the list starts, I say, "Thank you.

318
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:50,630
Now tell me one thing I did well."

319
00:14:51,610 --> 00:14:52,920
And what does the voice say, Ben?

320
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:54,890
Does it find one good thing, today?

321
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:56,980
Nothing, Mia.

322
00:14:57,680 --> 00:14:59,770
It goes quiet, because it does not know how.

323
00:15:00,589 --> 00:15:01,500
So I answer for it.

324
00:15:02,250 --> 00:15:02,980
"I called my mother.

325
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,420
That was good." One thing.

326
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:07,060
One thing is enough.

327
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:08,820
Today, I did enough.

328
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,180
That is the sentence.

329
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:11,640
And then I sleep.

330
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:15,680
It is Franklin's question from our last episode, actually.

331
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:16,860
What good did I do today?

332
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,340
I want to try that tonight, Ben.

333
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,980
Because my night list is long, and it never has a good thing on it.

334
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:25,180
My second idea is a letter.

335
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:26,999
You told me about it, actually.

336
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,790
A letter to yourself, from a kind friend.

337
00:15:30,680 --> 00:15:31,340
The letter, Mia.

338
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:31,900
Yes.

339
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:36,620
After my friend's sentence, I wrote myself a letter, as my friend.

340
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:39,640
"Dear Ben, you lost a job.

341
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:41,380
It happens to good people.

342
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:43,240
You are good at your work.

343
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,980
Take a week, then start." I read it every morning for a month.

344
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:50,280
Kristin Neff actually suggests this.

345
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:51,940
Did it feel silly, Ben?

346
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:57,880
Writing a letter to yourself, from a friend who is you, and reading it with your coffee every morning?

347
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:00,440
For three days, Mia.

348
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,460
On day four, it felt true.

349
00:16:03,460 --> 00:16:04,860
I found a job in two months.

350
00:16:05,350 --> 00:16:06,900
The letter did not find the job.

351
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:10,060
But the letter got me out of bed, and I found it.

352
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:14,820
"The letter got me out of bed." Ben, I want to write one tonight.

353
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:19,440
Because I can be that friend for Anna in five minutes on the phone.

354
00:16:19,460 --> 00:16:20,680
Five minutes is enough.

355
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:24,400
So I can be that friend for me on paper.

356
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,200
Same words.

357
00:16:25,530 --> 00:16:26,410
Same kindness.

358
00:16:26,780 --> 00:16:27,630
Different address.

359
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:30,040
Do you have a third idea?

360
00:16:30,060 --> 00:16:32,220
Something for our listeners who are learning English?

361
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:33,880
Yes, Mia.

362
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:37,220
Because this is where the voice is loudest for learners.

363
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,520
You say a sentence in English.

364
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,240
One word is wrong.

365
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:42,540
And the voice says, "See?

366
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:43,990
You cannot speak.

367
00:16:44,620 --> 00:16:48,660
Everyone noticed." I hear this from learners every week.

368
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:52,140
And I want to say, clearly, that voice is lying.

369
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:53,820
It is lying, Ben.

370
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:56,720
One wrong word is one wrong word.

371
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:59,300
The person you were talking to understood you.

372
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:02,000
They did not go home and think about your mistake.

373
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:03,620
They thought about their dinner.

374
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:05,840
One conversation is enough.

375
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,500
Only you are still thinking about the word.

376
00:17:09,190 --> 00:17:11,440
"They thought about their dinner." Yes, Mia.

377
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:14,960
When you make a mistake in Spanish, I do not remember it.

378
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,380
I remember that you talked to me in Spanish.

379
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,780
That is what people remember.

380
00:17:19,820 --> 00:17:20,360
The trying.

381
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:21,700
Not the mistake.

382
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:26,480
So for everyone learning English, here is a kind sentence for today.

383
00:17:26,490 --> 00:17:27,100
"I spoke.

384
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:31,910
That is enough." Not "I spoke perfectly." "I spoke.

385
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:36,100
That is enough." Say it after every conversation.

386
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,430
Today, I spoke.

387
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,760
That is enough for today.

388
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:42,520
It is true, and the voice hates true things.

389
00:17:42,910 --> 00:17:46,720
"The voice hates true things." And one last idea, Mia.

390
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:50,040
It is for the people who think they do not deserve kindness.

391
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:51,940
"Other people deserve it.

392
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:53,020
I do not.

393
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:58,280
My mistakes are worse." That is the voice again, wearing a serious coat.

394
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,490
Today, that voice is loud for many people.

395
00:18:02,209 --> 00:18:04,580
Everyone's voice says their mistakes are worse, Ben.

396
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,340
Everyone.

397
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,390
Anna's voice says it.

398
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:09,280
Your voice says it.

399
00:18:09,400 --> 00:18:10,980
My voice says it.

400
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,840
So it cannot be true for all of us.

401
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,770
It is just what the voice says.

402
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,180
You are not the exception.

403
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:19,920
You are a person, and persons get kindness.

404
00:18:20,429 --> 00:18:21,260
That is the rule.

405
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,200
"Persons get kindness.

406
00:18:23,750 --> 00:18:27,280
That is the rule." Mia, that is our message today.

407
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,600
There is a voice in your head, and it is not kind.

408
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:36,559
It says "always" and "never" and "not enough." And it is lying.

409
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:40,640
A mistake is one thing, on one day.

410
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:41,940
You are not the mistake.

411
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,360
So talk to yourself like a friend.

412
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:45,840
It is not weak.

413
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:50,300
It is the thing that lets you try again tomorrow.

414
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:52,240
The thing that lets you try again tomorrow.

415
00:18:52,990 --> 00:18:58,260
Ben, let's repeat today's important words, slowly, because our listeners want to remember them.

416
00:18:59,560 --> 00:18:59,960
Kind.

417
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:01,260
Good to someone.

418
00:19:01,940 --> 00:19:02,660
Be kind.

419
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,200
Kind to yourself.

420
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:05,820
Mistake.

421
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,540
Something that went wrong.

422
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,060
I made a mistake.

423
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:11,900
A mistake is not a person.

424
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:13,260
Friend.

425
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:15,360
A person you like and trust.

426
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:17,500
Talk to yourself like a friend.

427
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:19,780
Today.

428
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:21,380
This day, not always.

429
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:23,080
Today is a mix.

430
00:19:24,340 --> 00:19:24,780
Enough.

431
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,590
As much as is needed.

432
00:19:27,260 --> 00:19:28,050
I did enough.

433
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:29,600
That is enough.

434
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:31,460
Kind.

435
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:32,740
Mistake.

436
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:34,220
Friend.

437
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:35,680
Today.

438
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:37,240
Enough.

439
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:39,800
Five kind words.

440
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:41,080
And one big idea.

441
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,510
Talk to yourself like a friend.

442
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:47,540
Now, Mia, do you have a question for our listeners?

443
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,700
Yes, Ben.

444
00:19:48,780 --> 00:19:50,930
Everyone listening, here is my question.

445
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:54,670
What is one kind sentence you can say to yourself today?

446
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,400
Not a big one.

447
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:57,820
A small one.

448
00:19:57,850 --> 00:19:58,390
"I spoke.

449
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:05,920
That is enough." "I was tired because I worked." "One test is one test." Write it in the comments.

450
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,840
Today, one kind sentence is enough.

451
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:12,920
Reading those sentences is a kind thing for us, too.

452
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,180
And sometimes we borrow them.

453
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:16,500
Sometimes we borrow them.

454
00:20:17,260 --> 00:20:20,620
And if this episode helped you, please subscribe to Two Cups English.

455
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,200
We make a new episode every few days.

456
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:27,640
Slow English, simple words, and one true story each time.

457
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,709
The full text of this episode is in the description.

458
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,320
And if you missed some words today, that is fine.

459
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,720
You listened today.

460
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,840
That is enough.

461
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,580
Thank you for spending this time with us.

462
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:41,960
Maybe you had a hard day.

463
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,120
Maybe you made a mistake.

464
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:46,360
Maybe the voice is loud right now.

465
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:49,740
Here is what I would say to a friend, so I am saying it to you.

466
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,120
It's okay.

467
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:52,320
It happens.

468
00:20:53,060 --> 00:20:54,000
You are still here.

469
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:55,500
Have some tea.

470
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:57,680
Be kind to yourself today.

471
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,420
This is Ben.

472
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:01,100
And this is Mia.

473
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:03,200
This was Two Cups English.

474
00:21:04,040 --> 00:21:05,220
Be kind to yourself.

475
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,020
We will see you next time.

